@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</h1>

<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> It is a requirement that the Blazor Ramp Core <span class="code-span">core-live-region.js</span> script, <span class="code-span">LiveRegionService</span>, and
    associated <span class="code-span">&lt;AnnouncementHistory /&gt;</span> component are added alongside this component’s specific
    requirements (two stylesheet references in this instance).
</p>
<p>
    You do not need to add the BlazorRamp.Core package separately, as BlazorRamp.Core is included as a transitive package, you only need to add the packages that contain the components
    that you wish to use i.e the <b>BlazorRamp.DataTable</b> NuGet package.<br />
    <strong>Note: </strong> This package also makes use of the BlazorRamp.BusyIndicator NuGet so this will be included as a transitive package, but you will need to add its stylesheet as
    along side the other as described below.
    
</p>
<p>
    Please follow the instructions in the <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Getting_Started}{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">@GlobalValues.Getting_Started_Name - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</a>
    ensuring that in the <span class="code-span">&lt;head&gt;</span> section you also add both the Data Table and Busy Indicator stylesheets as follows:
</p>
<CodeBox CodeBlock="@DataTableSnippets.Add_Data_Table_Style_Sheets" AriaLabel="Add data table stylesheet code block" />


